  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">NIHR HPSR-PA - Does consolidated procurement influence affordable access to medicines? An Indonesian experiment (Transparency International Global Health component)</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Transparency International Global Health (TIGH), part of Transparency International UK, is the downstream collaborator on this NIHR Global Health Policy and Systems Research project (PROmeds), led by Universitas Pancasila in Indonesia and funded by the UK Department of Health and Social Care (DHSC) as Official Development Assistance. The project examines how changes to Indonesia&apos;s medicine procurement system affect the price, availability and governance of medicines under the national health insurance scheme. TIGH contributes anti-corruption expertise and supports the project by helping to sort, structure and analyse the procurement data.</narrative>
  </description>
